(D5 — Discrepancy 5 repro: `Send signal` hands the pid straight to kill(2)
 (LANGUAGE.md:4156-4157), so pid 0 (the caller's process group) and pid -1
 (every process this uid may signal) are reachable from an ordinary Vox
 program with no diagnostic and no guard.
 SAFETY: signal 0 only. The kernel delivers nothing for signal 0 — it does
 the permission check and returns — so running this repro is inert. The
 finding is that both lines succeed: with `9` in place of `0` the second
 one would kill every process this user owns.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/D5.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   kill(2) accepted the broadcast pid
)
Send signal 0 to process -1.
On error print "pid -1 was rejected".
print "kill(2) accepted the broadcast pid".
